restructure format:\n\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    target = record\n    max_chars = self.max_message_chars\n    if max_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n        message = record.getMessage()\n        if len(message) > max_chars:\n            target = copy.copy(record)\n            target.msg = self._truncate_message(message, max_chars)\n            target.args = None\n            target.message = target.msg  # not needed; super().format recomputes\n    msg = super().format(target)\n    if \"\\n\" in msg and target.message:\n        prefix = msg[: msg.find(target.message)]\n        msg = msg.replace(\"\\n\", \"\\n\" + prefix)\n    if self.use_color:\n        color = _LEVEL_COLORS.get(record.levelno)\n        if color:\n            msg = f\"{color}{msg}{_COLOR_RESET}\"\n    return msg\n```\n\nNote `getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True` — for value 1, `1 is not True` → True, so truncation applies. Good, spec says only exactly True.\n\nCareful: msg.find(target.message) — target.message is truncated message that includes \"...<omitted>...\" and possibly newlines from original; the prefix search still fine.\n\nEdge: record.getMessage() calls str(record.msg) % record.args; if msg formatting raises, base formatter would too. Fine.\n\nTruncation:\n```python\n_TRUNCATION_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\n\ndef _truncate_message(message, max_chars):\n    keep = max_chars - len(_TRUNCATION_MARKER)\n    head = (keep + 1) // 2\n    tail = keep - head\n    return message[:head] + _TRUNCATION_MARKER + (message[len(message) - tail:] if tail else \"\")\n```\nCheck budget 32: marker len = 15. keep = 17. head = 9, tail = 8. msg[:9] + marker + msg[-8:] → total 9+15+8 = 32. ✓ matches example.\n\nAlso spec says marker counts toward budget; if max_chars small (>=32) keep>=17 fine.\n\nAlso __init__ validation:\n```python\nif max_message_chars is not None:\n    if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstanc